  "readme": [
    "SYNTHETIC CATALOGUE \u2014 a test fixture, NOT sourcing truth.",
    "",
    "Every part below is invented to exercise the selection engine: there is one that qualifies,",
    "and one for each way a part can fail (the OTHER family's clock, 5 V part, unplaceable",
    "package, no published phase noise, too noisy, single-sourced). The MPNs are deliberately",
    "prefixed FIXTURE- so they can never be mistaken for parts anyone researched or can order.",
    "",
    "FIXTURE-OSC-24M576-WRONGFAMILY is the interesting one. 24.576 MHz is a perfectly good",
    "CS43131 MCLK \u2014 the DAC accepts it for every rate the product supports \u2014 and it is the",
    "cheapest, deepest-stocked, most-sourced oscillator here. It still has to be rejected for the",
    "44.1 kHz family, because the SAI cannot divide it to an exact 64 x 44100 bit clock",
    "(24.576e6 / 2.8224e6 = 8.707...). That is a constraint belonging to the MCU's serial port,",
    "not to the DAC, which is exactly the distinction an earlier version of this spec got wrong.",
    "",
    "The real catalogue replaces this file wholesale once distributor credentials exist: the",
    "fetcher pulls every part in a category from TME / Mouser / Digi-Key, and the engine filters",
    "it with exactly the same constraints exercised here. Nothing about the engine changes when",
    "the data becomes real \u2014 which is the point of testing it against a fixture first.",
    "",
    "Attribute names match what parametric search returns (frequency_hz, supply_mv_max, package,",
    "phase_noise_dbc_1khz, channels, break_before_make, max_freq_hz), because the constraints in",
    "dap-hw-spec are written against that vocabulary rather than an invented one.",
    "",
    "The battery and bluetooth categories exist because several constraints on those parts are",
    "LICENSING constraints wearing electrical clothing, and they are the ones a price-first",
    "filter gets wrong. FIXTURE-CELL-1200-SOLDERTAB is the cheapest cell with the deepest stock",
    "and the largest capacity, and it has to lose: solder tabs mean no spare battery and no",
    "Art. 11 user-replaceability. FIXTURE-CELL-1100-BARE is cheaper still and would transfer",
    "UN 38.3 and IEC 62133-2 certification from the cell vendor to us. FIXTURE-BT-BARE-SOC is",
    "half the price of the qualified module and costs a full Bluetooth qualification programme."
  ],
